                  <provenance cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_484">Salisbury, Wiltshire. Cathedral
                        church of St Mary the Virgin; see removed from Sherborne in 1078</orgName><p>Note probably by one of Parker's scribes: 'Hic ipsus est liber
                        quem Alwredus Rex misit ad ecclesiam Syreburnensem'. From this, M. R. James
                        deduced that 'it may perhaps be fair to conclude that the book came to
                        Parker from Sherborne'. However, there is a letter from Bishop Jewel to
                        accompany the gift to Parker of an Anglo-Saxon manuscript from Salisbury
                        which is bound up with the Anglo-Saxon Pastoral Care which is now CUL Ii.2.4
                        (q.v.). However, that manuscript is in an Exeter script and is too big a
                        book for the volume 'as thick as the Communion booke' that Jewel describes.
                        The presence of the Parkerian note in this manuscript suggests this is the
                        one Jewel sent from Salisbury.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Matthew Parker (1504--1575).</provenance>
               </history>
